1 second per test
O_DIRECT supported on this platform for open_datasync and open_sync.

Compare file sync methods using one 8kB write:
(in "wal_sync_method" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)
        open_datasync                       260.240 ops/sec    3843 usecs/op
        fdatasync                           730.768 ops/sec    1368 usecs/op
        fsync                               196.191 ops/sec    5097 usecs/op
        fsync_writethrough                              n/a
        open_sync                           199.144 ops/sec    5021 usecs/op

Compare file sync methods using two 8kB writes:
(in "wal_sync_method" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)
        open_datasync                       133.397 ops/sec    7496 usecs/op
        fdatasync                           752.413 ops/sec    1329 usecs/op
        fsync                               195.248 ops/sec    5122 usecs/op
        fsync_writethrough                              n/a
        open_sync                            97.392 ops/sec   10268 usecs/op

Compare open_sync with different write sizes:
(This is designed to compare the cost of writing 16kB in different write
open_sync sizes.)
         1 * 16kB open_sync write           196.665 ops/sec    5085 usecs/op
         2 *  8kB open_sync writes           97.478 ops/sec   10259 usecs/op
         4 *  4kB open_sync writes           40.994 ops/sec   24394 usecs/op
         8 *  2kB open_sync writes           23.454 ops/sec   42637 usecs/op
        16 *  1kB open_sync writes           12.151 ops/sec   82300 usecs/op

